Chapter: MathLib

 To square gives the product of a number with itself.
 To cube gives a number raised to the third power.
 To math-abs gives the absolute value of an integer.
 To math-min gives the smaller of two integers.
 To math-max gives the larger of two integers.
 To math-clamp gives an integer constrained to the given lower and upper bounds.
 To math-mod gives the remainder after integer division.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  square : Integer -> Integer
  square (x) = x * x

  cube : Integer -> Integer
  cube (x) = x * x * x

  helper : Integer -> Integer
  helper (x) = x + 1

Section: Common Helpers
  math-abs : Integer -> Integer
  math-abs (n) = if n < 0 then -n else n

  math-min : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  math-min (a) (b) = if a < b then a else b

  math-max : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  math-max (a) (b) = if a > b then a else b

  math-clamp : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  math-clamp (lo) (hi) (v) = if v < lo then lo else if v > hi then hi else v

  math-mod : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  math-mod (a) (b) = a - (a / b) * b

